            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0343" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">612.119/2859: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dyer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-12T11:00:00-07:23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1920—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:57 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Government of Sonora through Presidents Municipal Figueroa of Nogales, Sonora has
                    made application on form which I am forwarding today for permission to export
                    from United States 10,000 rifles and pistols and 2,000,000 cartridges, Remington
                    or Winchester, specifications to be supplied later. If not contrary to policy of
                    Department I urge favorable action, notification by wire.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dyer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
